<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="L-nicotianamine biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-5957" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Ubiquitous Plant Pathways (UPP) that was generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are thought to be present in all or most land plants. All UPP pathways are automatically imported into databases regardless of Pathologic predictions. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; |FRAME: CPD-463| is an unusual amino acid that is ubiquitous throughout the plant kingdom. It is a chelator of several divalent transition metals. Several studies have shown that |FRAME: CPD-463| is involved in long distance transport of metal ions such as iron and manganese, and that it is directly associated with the regulation of metal transfer within cells |CITS: [12782722]| and the maintenance of Fe homeostasis |CITS: [REICHMAN02]|. |FRAME: CPD-463|, which is present in all plant organs, is not secreted and is only involved in iron-trafficking internally |CITS: [10069850]|. Studies with transgenic |FRAME: TAX-4097| plants have shown that |FRAME: CPD-463| deficiency interferes with normal flower morphogenesis |CITS: [12782722]|.</Description>
